Define the current increment before deepening work: its authorized outcome, claims, supported inputs, and acceptance evidence. Settle every decision and valid finding that can change it; record later branches as fog or follow-up. Treat a pass as stale when the candidate or its evidence dependencies change; completion requires every selected review focus to have a clean latest pass on the same final revision. When complexity grows, adapt the claim, reviewer focus, and adjudication boundary; a cycle, time, token, or reviewer-count limit is not a completion criterion.
